# Fichero Release Notes

## 0.1.0.dev1 – In Progress
- Introduced new windows for Plans, Projects, and Prompts.
- Refactored Director.py:
  - Transitioned the backend to operate solely on Python, making REDIS and Celery optional for HPC/Linux environments.
  - Implemented multiprocessing for CPU-intensive tasks when processing a single folder, significantly enhancing performance.
  - Refactored director.py into various components to make it easier to understand.
  - Wrote a workflow backend, a monitoring backend, shared data for encrypted API keys and settings.
- Redesigned the plans format to remove dependency on Weasel, and subsequently eliminated the Weasel backend.
- Refactored tools to be called as function calls, not as new processes.
- Ran on 50 folders, encompassing a total of 7,992 images, as part of the [Archivo Afro](https://upenn.app.box.com/s/ezpp32x9p0yps244buzweyqfyn67h5l)
- Integrated rembg for AI-based background removal, which is an optional feature. Works great on many images, but not all. If rembg is unavailable, Fichero defaults to contour-based background removal. The GUI automatically disables the AI background removal option on Mac if rembg is not installed, and other platforms where rembg/scikit-image may encounter issues.
- Made the use of ultralytics in crop.py optional to facilitate Mac builds. Introduced a YOLO_AVAILABLE flag to verify YOLO's availability. Implemented a fallback to contour-based cropping when YOLO is not accessible. Modified crop_with_yolo() to return None if YOLO is unavailable. Enhanced crop_batch() to manage YOLO loading somewhat smoothly.
- Revised Activity Monitor to ensure only one instance can be active at a time.
-- Added fichero/utils/icon_utils.py: Platform-aware icon utility. Uses SF Symbols (via PyObjC/AppKit) on macOS, falls back to emoji on other platforms. Provides get_stop_icon(), get_refresh_icon(), get_add_icon(), get_remove_icon(), etc. Includes test script for verification. Requires pyobjc-framework-Cocoa on macOS. 

